@startuml Tourist_Create_Itinerary_SSD

actor "Tourist" as Tourist
participant "UI: Create Itinerary" as UI
participant "Database" as DB
participant "S3 Storage" as S3

== View Create Itinerary Page ==

Tourist -> UI: Access create itinerary page
activate UI

UI -> DB: Fetch all sites
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return sites list
deactivate DB

UI -> DB: Fetch user's itineraries
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return user itineraries
deactivate DB

UI --> Tourist: Display:\n- Create form (name, image, site selection)\n- My Itineraries list
deactivate UI

== Search and Filter Sites ==

Tourist -> UI: Enter search term or select category filter
activate UI

UI -> UI: Filter sites by:\n- Search (site name)\n- Category (all, church, museum, etc.)

UI --> Tourist: Display filtered available sites
deactivate UI

== Select Sites ==

Tourist -> UI: Click site to add to itinerary
activate UI

UI -> UI: Add site to selected list

alt Site is inside Fort Santiago
    UI -> DB: Check user preference\n(hideFortSantiagoModal)
    activate DB
    DB --> UI: Return preference
    deactivate DB
    
    alt Modal not disabled
        UI --> Tourist: Show Fort Santiago notice:\n"Entrance fee required"
        Tourist -> UI: Click "I Understand"
        
        opt "Don't show this again" checked
            UI -> DB: Save preference\n(hideFortSantiagoModal: true)
            activate DB
            deactivate DB
        end
    end
end

UI --> Tourist: Update selected sites list
deactivate UI

== Upload Cover Image ==

Tourist -> UI: Click "Upload Image"
activate UI

UI --> Tourist: Show file picker

Tourist -> UI: Select image file

UI -> S3: Upload image
activate S3
S3 --> UI: Return S3 URL
deactivate S3

UI --> Tourist: Display image preview
deactivate UI

== Delete Cover Image ==

Tourist -> UI: Click delete image icon
activate UI

UI --> Tourist: Show confirmation

Tourist -> UI: Confirm delete

UI -> S3: Delete image from storage
activate S3
deactivate S3

UI --> Tourist: Remove image preview
deactivate UI

== Create Itinerary ==

Tourist -> UI: Enter name and click "Create"
activate UI

UI -> UI: Validate:\n- Name required\n- At least 1 site selected

alt Input valid
    alt Online
        UI -> DB: Save itinerary record
        activate DB
        DB --> UI: Itinerary created
        deactivate DB
        
        UI -> UI: Reset form
        
        UI --> Tourist: Show success message,\nrefresh My Itineraries list
    else Offline
        UI --> Tourist: Show offline modal:\n"Creating itineraries requires internet"
    end
else Input invalid
    UI --> Tourist: Show validation error
end

deactivate UI

== Edit Itinerary ==

Tourist -> UI: Click "Edit" on itinerary
activate UI

UI -> UI: Load itinerary data:\n- Name\n- Image\n- Selected sites

UI --> Tourist: Display form with current data

Tourist -> UI: Modify details and click "Update"

UI -> UI: Validate input

alt Input valid
    alt Online
        UI -> DB: Update itinerary record
        activate DB
        DB --> UI: Itinerary updated
        deactivate DB
        
        UI -> UI: Reset form
        
        UI --> Tourist: Show success message,\nrefresh list
    else Offline
        UI --> Tourist: Show offline modal
    end
else Input invalid
    UI --> Tourist: Show validation error
end

deactivate UI

== Delete Itinerary ==

Tourist -> UI: Click "Delete" on itinerary
activate UI

UI --> Tourist: Show confirmation dialog

Tourist -> UI: Confirm delete

alt Online
    UI -> DB: Remove itinerary record
    activate DB
    DB --> UI: Itinerary deleted
    deactivate DB
    
    UI --> Tourist: Refresh My Itineraries list
else Offline
    UI --> Tourist: Show offline modal:\n"Deleting requires internet"
end

deactivate UI

== View Itinerary Details ==

Tourist -> UI: Click on itinerary to expand
activate UI

UI --> Tourist: Display:\n- Cover image\n- List of sites with descriptions\n- Total sites count

deactivate UI

@enduml
